{"id":"expl:scripts/crib-cost-report.mjs@L84","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"scripts/crib-cost-report.mjs","span":{"start":84,"end":85}},"file":"scripts/crib-cost-report.mjs","span":{"start":84,"end":85},"lang":"javascript","hash":"blake3:13bcb16b4e2219f20febd7db76bdcbeeee98abf944cbcaa469a21db1e243cf35","meta":{"text":"Reconciliation: does the shared rate model reproduce the panel's reported cost? If it drifts hard,\nthe rates are wrong (or a bucket is mis-mapped) and every downstream claim is suspect — surface it."}}
{"id":"expl:scripts/crib-cost-report.mjs@L99","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"scripts/crib-cost-report.mjs","span":{"start":99,"end":106}},"file":"scripts/crib-cost-report.mjs","span":{"start":99,"end":106},"lang":"javascript","hash":"blake3:401f7c9fa8c00ecc7fbbccec9d1b520b41394a3b6d4b02098a47e08be169788d","meta":{"text":"Two cost lenses, kept separate on purpose:\n- list-rate  : what the run WOULD cost on API pay-as-you-go, from the shared rate model. Here\ncache-read is 0.1x input — cheap, but NOT free, so more cache-read tokens still add up.\n- reported   : the figure the /usage panel actually showed (subscription/plan billing). On a Max/Pro\nplan, marginal cache-read is effectively subsidized, which is why the same run can be\nfar cheaper than its list-rate equivalent.\nThe \"more tokens, less money\" claim must name its lens — it can be TRUE on a plan yet FALSE at list\nrates. Judging it on the wrong basis is exactly the trap this tool exists to prevent."}}
